 height="15" topLeftX="850" topLeftY="510" type="text"><content verticalAlign="top" fontSize="10" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(31, 41, 55, 1)" bold="true" lineSpacing="multiple:1.15" textAlign="right" wrap="false"><p>205</p></content></shape></data><note><content><p>RK42 audits nine public construct-level datasets against the seven frozen eligibility requirements, label-free, before any outcome association.</p><p>None passes all seven: regulatory-grammar libraries fix the CDS, N-terminal fusions fix the leader and vary amino acids, and the one synonymous set is too small.</p><p>The branch decision is B3: build prospective independent data via DBTL/wet-lab, which requires user budget and timeline approval.</p></content></note></slide>
